      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 53-year-old woman was referred urgently to the urology department with a history of worsening right renal angle pain and associated hematuria. Further investigations revealed the presence of a primary non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) invading the posterior chest wall with an associated vaginal metastasis. To our knowledge, this is only the second case report in the literature of a vaginal metastasis from NSCLC."},
